Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?kms:=20the=20door=20v0=20(E08),=20the=20checks?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20of=20design/keys=20=C2=A73=20in=20order,=20cryptography=20as?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20a=20backend?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sharness_ai/kms/: KMS on the door kit (init, identity, unwrap, seal_to, destroy;
GET /v0/policy and /v0/hello from Door), checks 1 to 8 in the design's order,
the per-agent kms rows of the policy (one session, one agent), nonces kept
until ts + 2 min, max_uses, a fresh approval for write and seal_to, keys
handed over as bytearrays and zeroed before the answer. Crypto.py is the
backend interface; the only backend, NoCrypto, answers 501, because the
envelope needs AES-256-GCM, which neither the standard library nor the
openssl 3.0 command line provides. tests/unit/kms/test_kms.py: one test
per check, with a test-only backend; every key made inside the test.
